    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\"><span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"2\">Level 2 - Beginner</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span><span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Strings: reverse twice</span><a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/reverse-words-in-a-string/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 151</a></div>\n  <h1>Reverse Words in a String</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">Insight in one line: reversing the whole string puts the words in the right order but spells each one backwards; reversing each word again fixes the spelling. Do it with a write pointer that trails the read pointer and the extra spaces vanish in the same pass. O(n) time, O(1) extra space when the buffer is mutable.</p>\n"
